</surname><given-names>DD</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Twickler</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></string-name></person-group>. <article-title>Effect of maternal obesity on the ultrasound detection of anomalous fetuses</article-title>. <source>Obstet Gynecol</source><year>2009</year>;<volume>113</volume>:<fpage>1001</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>7</lpage>. <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/AOG.0b013e3181a1d2f5</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19384114</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R13"><label>13</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><string-name><surname>Thornburg</surname><given-names>LL</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Miles</surname><given-names>K</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Ho</surname><given-names>M</given-names></string-name>, <etal>et al</etal></person-group>. <article-title>Fetal anatomic evaluation in the overweight and obese gravida</article-title>. <source>Ultrasound Obstet Gynecol</source><year>2009</year>;<volume>33</volume>:<fpage>670</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>5</lpage>. <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/uog.6401</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19479682</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R14"><label>14</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><string-name><surname>Szabo</surname><given-names>TL</given-names></string-name></person-group>. <part-title>Chapter 1 - Introduction</part-title>. In: <source>Diagnostic ultrasound imaging: inside out</source>. <edition>2nd edn</edition>. <publisher-name>Academic Press</publisher-name>, <year>2014</year>: <fpage>1</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>37</lpage>. <uri xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/B978012396487800001X">http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/B978012396487800001X</uri></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R15"><label>15</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><string-name><surname>Nelson</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Pretorius</surname><given-names>DH</given-names></string-name></person-group>. <article-title>The Doppler signal: where does it come from and what does it mean?</article-title><source>AJR Am J Roentgenol</source><year>1988</year>;<volume>151</volume>:<fpage>439</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>47</lpage>. <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2214/ajr.151.3.439</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2970215</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R16"><label>16</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><string-name><surname>Jensen</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></string-name></person-group>. <article-title>Medical ultrasound imaging</article-title>. <source>Prog Biophys Mol Biol</source><year>2007</year>;<volume>93</volume>:<fpage>153</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>65</lpage>. <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.pbiomolbio.2006.07.025</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17092547</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R17"><label>17</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><string-name><surname>Wells</surname><given-names>PNT</given-names></string-name></person-group>. <article-title>Ultrasonic imaging of the human body</article-title>. <source>Rep Prog Phys</source><year>1999</year>;<volume>62</volume>:<fpage>671</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>722</lpage>. <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1088/0034-4885/62/5/201</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R18"><label>18</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><string-name><surname>Carson</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></string-name></person-group>. <article-title>Biomedical ultrasonics. By P.N.T. Wells, Ph.D., Academic Press, Inc. London, Copyright 1977. 635 pages. $46.90</article-title>. <source>J Clin Ultrasound</source><year>1978</year>;<volume>6<